  <static seed="1878" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/FractionApplication/FractionAdditionWordProblems10.pg">
    <statement><p>Briana walked <m>{{\frac{1}{12}}}</m> of a mile in the morning, and then walked <m>{{\frac{3}{8}}}</m> of a mile in the afternoon. How far did Briana walk altogether?</p>
<p>Briana walked a total of <fillin characters="11" name="AnSwEr0001"/> of a mile.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>{\frac{11}{24}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>This is an addition problem.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 
\begin{aligned}[t]
   {{\frac{1}{12}}} + {{\frac{3}{8}}} 
      \amp = \frac{1 \cdot 2}{12 \cdot 2}+\frac{3 \cdot 3}{8 \cdot 3} \\
      \amp = \frac{2}{24} + \frac{9}{24} \\
      \amp = \frac{2+9}{24} \\
      
      \amp = {{\frac{11}{24}}}
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
<p>Briana walked a total of <m>{{\frac{11}{24}}}</m> miles altogether.</p>
</solution>
